# CODEOWNERS — human ownership of the merge gates.
#
# Merges are mechanical: a PR merges when the required checks go green, with no
# human necessarily reading the code. That makes the paths below load-bearing —
# the pipeline must not be able to edit the things that check it. GitHub requires
# a review from the owner below before any change to these paths can merge, even
# under auto-merge. Keep this in sync with the required status checks in branch
# protection.
#
# For this to bind, the human must (once) enable branch protection on the default
# branch with "Require review from Code Owners" turned on. See the README.

# CI (hard gate), the review check + its prompt, the CODEOWNERS file itself, and
# the runner scripts all live under .github/ — one rule covers them.
/.github/                    @GrimsVerk

# Pre-commit (git-level gate).
/.pre-commit-config.yaml     @GrimsVerk

# Any root-level CODEOWNERS, in case one is added later.
/CODEOWNERS                  @GrimsVerk
